{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:21.951795Z","id":"d5d25c036575c8d79a42b36bcd0ff037ca6859b8afc4a3eef1dcc021b6005f5b","body":{"detail":"With first-take ownership (spec 2026-10-08 M23), the collection's takes make the fixture's live agent the owner of the threads it is delivered, and GET .../threads then carries owner {handle, live, name, person} (spec section 19 item 6 lists owner as an expected additive field). Compared with the committed fixtures/single-owner-21.golden.json after removing every owner key, the regenerated golden is equal. The committed golden was not rewritten: whether to regenerate it now or let plan Task 25's comparison expect the field is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":877},"end":{"line":890},"content_hash":"e380f23f39bcb646c8d62dafd110ba3cb4e77b3435c48da23a69a1ad4d48704c"},"summary":"Regenerating the single-owner golden adds an owner field to 36 raw thread views; it is otherwise identical","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:47:38.362437Z","id":"109c814e8ac8b1e516d72bbf9ab9c4761630d3fc8e96a10da5cf0b40bcad63d0","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Ruled by the coordinator in the Task 15 review: the golden holds when it is identical once every owner key is removed (spec 2026-10-08 section 19 item 6 expects owner); the committed golden stays. Checked again at 1f0f12a: equal without owner, 36 owner values added.","supersedes":"d5d25c036575c8d79a42b36bcd0ff037ca6859b8afc4a3eef1dcc021b6005f5b","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.364409Z","id":"5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3","body":{"detail":"the_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor reruns api_artifacts, api_content, api_assets, api_threads and the api_live* modules with CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred, skipping the tests that read or change the home files or call synchronous store methods themselves. A stale skip name skips nothing and a new such test fails the rerun, which is loud; its >100 threshold only catches an empty filter. Content routes outside those modules (for example docs, approvals) are not rerun.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"f198c5e6916be4111196ec404f505223ad4ff56dca8f14c72e527349c488b94d"},"summary":"The Deferred-content rerun skips ten tests by name and adds about 5 s to the server suite; a renamed or new file-layout test needs the list kept by hand","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638796Z","id":"6dd9b4184d83df959232bb6b344eaeaa9fc421b9186650e7972ccaf426db8927","body":{"detail":"Mutation runs against crates/clax-server/tests (api_people, api_agent_auth, api_sessions, api_grants): sessionless_narrow keeping only the first narrowing (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, `Some(a) => a`) and proved_row refreshing a proved row of another harness (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:352) both pass every test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1281},"end":{"line":1333},"content_hash":"3e044e1505a04649ae16a0975ec1470709302b20b947a74e2fed155dd94e7268"},"suggested_fix":"Narrow two sessions to different locations and check a session-less request gets neither's excess; register with a proof of a claude session as codex and check a new row is made.","summary":"No test has two narrowed sessions, or a proof of a session of another harness","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.904951Z","id":"af8904b3c8011df4d0be08b5ca5635d3f9b1ca350dba70a8e87b8520764d4f22","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"api_people::every_live_narrowing_binds_a_request_naming_no_session narrows two sessions in both orders (catches the first-narrowing-only mutation); a_nested_agent_proving_its_parents_session_gets_its_own proves a session of another harness (a new codex row, not the proved claude one); the PID fallback and the join's wait are pinned by the tests named on 5d0c97a9 and 64fd9bb2. All eleven fix-round mutations are caught (target/t19a/mutations2.txt).","supersedes":"6dd9b4184d83df959232bb6b344eaeaa9fc421b9186650e7972ccaf426db8927","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657850Z","id":"d494907231a2d1935b8081788e7979574f0e7397cb8df554ac5b33d7d50c350b","body":{"detail":"Two mutations survive api_approvals::, api_threads::, shell_boot:: and api_events:: (83 tests). (1) In keep_approvers (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:583-588), Handles::Of(Some(p)) keeps approver for every connected person. (2) In boot.rs:196, the boot payload uses Handles::All for LAN viewers and anonymous callers. whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned asks only the owner, the approver, the author, a LAN viewer and no cookie, although its doc comment promises 'nor a connected person the thread does not concern'. Also, a decide_request that does not re-announce its thread (crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1959-1963) is caught only by a_declined_comment_leaves_its_thread_waiting_for_nothing hanging until nextest ends it at 120 s. Bound that event wait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2456},"end":{"line":2501},"content_hash":"dfadd941db10671133605410494e0f24a27d6f75ae13bb49301e7d238232a7fc"},"summary":"No test covers the approver rule for a connected person a thread does not concern, or for the boot payload","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.888794Z","id":"ae90aa83576fb59f9ba012d5b2a23ebcf555d5ec26cfa9bb6a7a51ed2b5f8efc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned now asks Mia, a connected person the thread does not concern, and reads the boot payload for every caller; event waits are bounded (within, 10 s). Evidence: three mutations each fail a test: Handles::Of(Some(p)) keeping the full state for every person (whose_approval_..., Mia), boot using Handles::All for everyone (whose_approval_..., Lucy's boot), and decide_request not re-announcing (a_declined_thread_..., held_state wait fails in 10 s).","supersedes":"d494907231a2d1935b8081788e7979574f0e7397cb8df554ac5b33d7d50c350b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641540Z","id":"a5c6889e1b5c9c0eaa0a3f6dfec7c2b08956b39d250f68a48f56e4d571e43b0a","body":{"detail":"Mutations run with the api_approvals, api_threads, shell_boot, api_events and api_inbox integration tests (104 tests). M6: concerned() (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:491-505) skips the thread's authors, so held_state reaches only the owner's inbox topic: all pass. M9: states_for gives Handles::All full(false), so the owner's own approval never reads mine ('waiting for your approval'): all pass. The tests hear held_state on the owner's topic only, and assert no mine for the owner only where Sam approves. Add a held_state read on Mia's (an author's) and Sam's (the approver's) inbox topics, and a thread waiting for the owner's approval read by the owner's browser with mine: true.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2471},"end":{"line":2635},"content_hash":"3a530416ffb32bdba7a4327552cfe89e361fc6ec4fe295a2b3d222256324a88d"},"summary":"Two mutations of the held-state rules survive: held_state reaching only the owner, and the owner's browser never reading mine","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.441755Z","id":"f52305d10af72a7703be0ffe62cbfd9bae4f92951fda88284c450c644a2124a0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed by new tests: api_approvals::the_approver_reads_its_own_decisions (Sam's decline reaches Sam's own stream with mine: true, and Mia's and the owner's) catches M6 (a decision reaches the owner alone); api_approvals::the_owner_reads_every_rows_state_and_mine_for_its_own_approval (the owner reads mine: true on Mia's thread to its agent) catches M7 (the owner never reads mine). Each mutation was restored by rewriting the file's bytes.","supersedes":"a5c6889e1b5c9c0eaa0a3f6dfec7c2b08956b39d250f68a48f56e4d571e43b0a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_gateway.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:30.468062Z","id":"8ece94f2fbd3b2a3cf18cad2caaf0beb6d1f703224d8a2222d0ec4bad7b22773","body":{"detail":"The case asks /api/artifacts/{hid}/approves-first with `tid`, a thread of the live page, so the handler's thread_of answers 404 whatever the gateway does. With the rule in crates/clax-server/src/extension.rs:238 changed to Rule::Any, `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_gateway` still passes (12 passed); only the unit table the_allowlist_names_each_route_and_the_artifact_it_needs_live fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":294},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"21e1c1ea62544ffdf9a9f1bb153dbf0886508b958631a37f7249d0338de4d19e"},"suggested_fix":"Make a thread on the published (non-live) artifact `hid` and ask approves-first for it: 404 from the gateway, 200 without it.","summary":"The approves-first refusal case would pass without the gateway's live-page check","tags":["review","test","task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_gateway.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:05:29.985434Z","id":"19f536a3c6b2e4142a70e651e632f400bab5d5000df5977f7f9a1596d4a5b416","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21d2a440","summary":"everything_else_is_refused now asks approves-first on the published page about that page's own thread (htid), so the handler would answer 200; only the gateway's live-page rule refuses it. Mutation: with the rule changed to Rule::Any the test fails; restored, api_gateway passes (12/12).","supersedes":"8ece94f2fbd3b2a3cf18cad2caaf0beb6d1f703224d8a2222d0ec4bad7b22773","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:04:52.464585Z","id":"1be89cf758c09e72d95aa30d0816bc005be1634c76dbf96ac920e4c82c5e29dd","body":{"detail":"Failure seen once: //crates/clax-server:integration__3 at commit 31b71b26, load about 6, assets upload answered 408 'request exceeded 2s' at api_timeout.rs:158 (expected 201). Three reruns (--runs_per_test=3) passed. Each request carries a 500 ms delay header against publish_timeout = 2 s, so any upload slower than 1.5 s under load fails. A wider timeout (or an injected clock for the timeout layer) would keep the test from depending on the machine's speed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"496b99fe92f67149664e5e8c9f732fb62dc0fe0e2a078f7286f57ea0928b665b"},"summary":"The publish-timeout test can fail on a slow machine: three uploads must each finish within a 2 s wall-clock timeout","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.816599Z","id":"7f8dfab537761624b025de18c8f7137c3b05e75e142056029869b83d5d00f0b5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The test moved to crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs, which every split test target compiles; the concern is recorded again there, with what the split changes.","supersedes":"5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/deferred.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844982Z","id":"4df6b70c7620a5595755894e7aacd6ddb2c73654f6082d34b7411a02cd96a1cf","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs:46-97, record 92c3be13.\n\nthe_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor reruns, of api_artifacts, api_content, api_assets, api_threads and the api_live* modules, those this test binary holds (all under Cargo; under Bazel, those its integration__N target was dealt, crates/clax-server/BUILD.bazel) with CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred, skipping the tests that read or change the home files or call synchronous store methods themselves. A stale skip name skips nothing and a new such test fails the rerun, which is loud. Under Cargo the >100 threshold catches an empty filter; under Bazel each held module must have one passing test in the rerun. holds() names each module by its clax_split cfg, so a module added to MODULES without a holds() arm is never rerun under Bazel. Content routes outside those modules (for example docs, approvals) are not rerun. Moved with the test from crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs (record 5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:217836344261c10bd08dc555b813e6df2823eb7c","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"569d77cbd123cd3f8ffa22e89e01e90fb12092dc5cf8113b12b5ec77ee5c7181"},"summary":"The Deferred-content rerun skips eleven tests by name and adds seconds to each server test target that holds a rerun module; a renamed or new file-layout test needs the list kept by hand, and a new module whose content routes should rerun needs adding to MODULES and holds()","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537113Z","id":"4d403064ab05092a6986360a1ff5da3310fbfb3d70b49e6c6dd2de15348a3348","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T15:12:24.892970Z","id":"1c02e0439f8611a55f0e2c5b805935dfe2531b2b6cbff4f1b4452c4de2327147","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of scripts/quality_gates.sh, cargo nextest failed api_linked::an_open_copy_holds_one_poll_there_however_often_the_sync_wakes at line 1211, assert_eq!(question_waiters(&rqid), 1): left 0, right 1, after five backstop wakes and sleeper.wait_for(BACKSTOP, 1). The same test passed alone natively (1.0 s) and in both Bazel runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__*. A sync wake that ends the remote poll and starts the next leaves a moment with no waiter.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1199},"end":{"line":1211},"content_hash":"e6dc063f675a42bfb961f462ba0419566aceba390032a7473f8a0d84053fcdf0"},"suggested_fix":"Wait until the count is 1 (or assert that it never exceeds 1 across the wakes) rather than reading it once.","summary":"The one-poll test reads the remote's waiter count at one instant, between polls it can be 0","tags":["tests","flaky","linked","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:13:49.995554Z","id":"57d9b52540a1fbe71903cdd3726993b6d112d883ab7b40d67fd365c331252abb","body":{"detail":"Failure: in 1 of 100 runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__4 (bazel test --runs_per_test=100 --local_test_jobs=12, the six integration targets at once and six CPU-bound processes beside them), line 1097 found linked.answered_there false on a question already answered (answered_via \"shell\", linked.sent true). The other 99 runs passed. The answer and the flag reach the local row apart, and the test reads the row once after the ask returns.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1096},"end":{"line":1097},"content_hash":"c7fad44d4bb1ee98b0eff4e53cdf0b1b3dcf044b6490f60f16ea0fdbcd387511"},"suggested_fix":"Wait until local_question shows answered_there (until(...)), or set the flag in the same write that closes the question.","summary":"a_local_ask_on_a_linked_artifact_is_asked_there_and_answered_from_there can read the local question answered before its answered_there flag is set","tags":["tests","flaky","linked","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_tool_call_ids.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:13:49.995884Z","id":"d549d9cc9ba409985c704ce0ec31c8e3784a8992ecb24f5b25e2c043065ad761","body":{"detail":"Failure: in 1 of 100 runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__4 under the load described on crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:1096, line 370 got {\"call_id\":null,\"recorded\":true,\"seq\":5} where the publish call's ID was expected. The daemon is no_grace() (CallIdWait with Duration::ZERO), so a report that arrives before the matching call is visible gets none; the test's back-dated event is 120 s before Utc::now(), a wall-clock reference. The other 99 runs passed. Not investigated further.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":348},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"6d8a705c757a6f0d3eee28930c98c3310f090bad67bd0376ff6beba330b95915"},"summary":"a_clock_step_back_hides_no_call failed once under heavy load: the hook's report found no call ID","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
